id: pm-beads-080q
title: beads validate and beads diff fail to register on pm-cli 2026.7.27 because each redeclares the host-owned --json global
description: "pm-cli 2026.7.27 (GH-719) makes the host reject any extension command whose flags shadow a host-owned global flag. beads validate and beads diff both declared { long: \"--json\" } in their flags arrays (VALIDATE_FLAGS and DIFF_FLAGS), so both commands failed to register against a real pm host. The suite never caught this because every smoke test built a hand-rolled api double that accepts all registrations unconditionally. Additionally, the audit:prod script used a bare 'npm audit --omit=dev' that fails with EALLOWSCRIPTS in project-scoped installs. Fix: drop both --json flag declarations, read the value from ctx.global.json in parseDiffOptions and the validate handler, rebuild the smoke suite on the SDK createExtensionTestHarness so pm's real activation engine validates registration, add a suite-wide guard, and fix audit:prod to strip npm_config_allow_scripts."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-27T05:14:42.040Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T23:10:18.340Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-27T22:41:16.496Z"
author: pi-agent
release: 2026.7.27
resolution: "Both commands re-register on pm-cli 2026.7.27 after dropping the shadowing --json declaration. Left unattributed on purpose: backdating it into 2026.7.27 would claim a cut release contained a fix it does not."
expected_result: "beads validate and beads diff register successfully under pm-cli 2026.7.27, with the changelog entry under Unreleased until the next release is cut."
actual_result: "Before the fix, redeclaring the host-owned --json global aborted registration at that command and dropped every later sibling, while --help still exited 0 with a misleading arity error (upstream pm-cli#772)."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T05:14:46.623Z",pi-agent,"Verified end-to-end: activation probe prints failed=[]; full suite 85/85 pass; release:check green. Also fixed pre-existing audit:prod EALLOWSCRIPTS bug."
  "2026-07-27T23:10:18.340Z",claude-code,"CORRECTION to this item's own retirement. It was first closed with NO release attribution on the conclusion that the v2026.07.27 tag was cut before PR #51 merged, which would have made the fix genuinely unreleased. That conclusion was WRONG and came from STALE LOCAL TAGS: I compared commit ordering in git log rather than checking tag containment, and the local tag set was behind. After git fetch --tags --force, git merge-base --is-ancestor b4c4df7 v2026.07.27 confirms the fix IS contained in v2026.07.27. Re-attributed to 2026.7.27 so the entry sits in the release that actually carried it rather than in Unreleased. The durable lesson: verify release membership with git merge-base --is-ancestor against a freshly fetched tag, never by eyeballing git log order."
close_reason: "Retired as shipped: the fix stopping beads validate and beads diff from shadowing the host-owned --json global merged today as PR #51, restoring registration under pm-cli 2026.7.27. Deliberately closed with NO release attribution, because the v2026.7.27 tag was cut before that merge -- the fix is genuinely unreleased and belongs in the Unreleased section."
body: ""
